===Etymology===
First attested in 1677.  From {{term|alkali|lang=en}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ar|en}} {{term|قلي|القلي|tr=al-qaly|ashes of the [[saltwort]]|lang=ar}}, from {{term|قلى|tr=qalā||to roast in a pan, fry|lang=ar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈæl.kəl.aɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ălˈkəlīn}}, {{IPA|/ˈæl.kə.laɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-alkaline.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[alkaline battery]].

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, or relating to an [[alkali]], one of a class of caustic bases.
# {{context|chemistry|lang=en}} Having a [[pH]] greater than 7.

